# Scoped to what the root Dockerfile actually builds: the MCP server image
# (apps/server + its one workspace dep, @learn-shell/contracts). Targeted
# COPY lines in the Dockerfile already avoid pulling in anything below, but
# excluding it here too keeps the build-context upload small and fast.

# Version control / CI meta — never needed inside the image.
.git
.github

# Root & per-package node_modules — reinstalled fresh in the builder stage
# from pnpm-lock.yaml. Shipping the host's copy in would also drag along
# whatever native binaries were built for the host's OS/arch, not the
# container's.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — regenerated by `pnpm --filter @learn-shell/server build`
# inside the builder stage. A stale host-built dist/ must never leak in
# ahead of that (and would otherwise shadow the freshly-built one for
# anyone iterating on the Dockerfile locally).
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo

# apps/web and packages/ui — this image is the MCP server only. Excluding
# them keeps their unrelated toolchain (Vite, sharp, onnxruntime-node, …)
# out of the build context entirely, so it can't become a failure mode for
# this image. If a future image needs the web app, add it back
# deliberately rather than deleting this line.
apps/web
packages/ui

# docs/media — 5MB+ of images for the docs site. Nothing the MCP server
# reads at runtime lives here (only docs/recipes/*.md and
# docs/LESSON-BLOCKS-v1.md do — see Dockerfile's COPY comments for why).
docs/media

# apps/server dev-only directory: drizzle migrations/studio metadata, not
# read by `tsc` (outside tsconfig.json's "src/**/*" include) or by the
# compiled MCP entrypoint (db pool is lazy — see db/client.ts — and never
# touches migration files).
apps/server/drizzle

# Local secrets / env files — DATABASE_URL etc. must come from the
# container's real environment (see docker/entrypoint.sh), never baked
# into a layer.
.env
.env.*
apps/server/.env

# Test / coverage artifacts.
coverage
.coverage
htmlcov

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
logs
